<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="53580" href="schedule/2022/fall/CMN/529/53580.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2022" href="schedule/2022.xml">2022</calendarYear><term id="120228" href="schedule/2022/fall.xml">Fall 2022</term><subject id="CMN" href="schedule/2022/fall/CMN.xml">Communication</subject><course id="529" href="schedule/2022/fall/CMN/529.xml">Seminar Communication Theory</course></parents><sectionNumber>4  </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Meta-Analysis in Communication</sectionTitle><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Meta-analysis is a quantitative approach to reviewing quantitative research. In this seminar, students will learn the difference between systematic reviews and meta-analyses, benefits and limitations of conducting a meta-analysis, and how to conduct a meta-analysis. Students must have completed a graduate level research methods course that covered quantitative methods and at least one statistics course prior to enrollment.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Open (Restricted)</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2022-08-22Z</startDate><endDate>2022-12-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="S5 ">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>02:00 PM</start><end>04:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>R      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>4103</roomNumber><buildingName>Lincoln Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Bigsby" firstName="E">Bigsby, E</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>